      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Yeah, the rule isn't complicated, but I was thinking about running demos for people who had never heard of the game before, and then thought about 'what if I had to explain everything in my second language?' and chose what was easiest to think through/explain without relying on English vocabulary. My thought is that simple logic (if/then or if/always as opposed if/when/then sort of stuff) and fewer mechanics that rely on explanation would be easier for running interpretation (as opposed to sitting down and translating the cards into another language... which eventually yall should totally do for sale in other countries!).",
